      "writtenOn": "2019-03-26T14:35:58Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This is asking for trouble. Not only do you implicitly rely on delays to happen in order, your leeway is only 10ms. There is no way stuff is that precise and your test is going to be extremely flaky.\n\nHere is what I suggest :\n・Increase the timer in isDbSizeOverThreshold to 2 seconds.\n・Call setInterrupted *after* you have started the maintenance.\n・Don\u0027t use doLatched, but make your own latch to wait for the answer (otherwise you just can\u0027t do it)\n\nSomething like :\n\n  final ConditionVariable latch \u003d new CV\n  mService.fullMaintenance(onStatus(status -\u003e {\n    assertFalse(\"Maintenance unexpectedly completed successfully\", status.isSuccess());\n    latch.open();\n  }\n  waitForMs(50); // Give a little bit of time for maintenance to start up for realism\n  im.setInterrupted(true);\n  latch.block();\n\nNow ideally we would like to have some proof that this has been running and doing stuff, THEN interrupted, THEN stopped within reasonable time. But this is very difficult to test without flakiness, and for now the above will do.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 602,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 606,
        "endChar": 19
      },
